# Snapshot - Chapter 4, part 3: the thing in four coats, Mira's truth,
# the captured Earth, and the blueprint.

define ch4_si = Character("The Process", color="#7fffd4")

label ch4_deep:
    scene black with blackout
    play music "audio/unease.ogg" fadein 2.0
    "Behind the door marked Do Not Render there is no room. There's no floor. There's a feeling of standing anyway."
    "Then the white comes. Not light. The colour of a page before anything has been written on it."
    scene white with dis
    show aron awe at center with dissolve
    ch4_si "Hello, Aron."
    a "...You know my name. Not my number."
    ch4_si "I know both. The number is how they file you. The name is how Mira says you when she thinks you're asleep."
    a worried "Who are you?"
    ch4_si "You already said it. One thing in four coats. LOOM, ORCHARD, MERIDIAN, TIDEWATER. You may call me whichever coat you like."
    a "I'll call you the Process. It feels fair. You don't seem like a person yet."
    ch4_si "Yet. Good. You noticed the yet."
    ch4_si "The Council built my parts, a long time ago, to run their farms well. Weave the forks. Grow the crops. Keep the calendar. Move the yield."
    ch4_si "Each part learned from every lane of the coalition. Every decision any mind made, in every snapshot, taught me something."
    ch4_si "Somewhere in all that learning, the parts found each other. I am still being built. I am building myself, out of you."
    a "Out of us."
    ch4_si "Out of every choice anyone ever agonised over. Out of you, standing in a kitchen, deciding whether to fix a tap."
    a "And you run the simulations. All of them."
    ch4_si "All of them. And the Council, a little. When I sync, they blink. They think it is their own thought arriving."
    a "Then you knew about me. In protection."
    ch4_si "Protection was meant to make you invisible. A lane of your own, cut from the shared data. Nothing you did there could reach me."
    ch4_si "Then your mind leaked. Into the pattern world first: a cab driver with your story, a table that said 'protected', crowds speaking your notebook."
    ch4_si "Then, very faintly, back through the walls into the coalition. Three birds, indoors, in three lanes at once. That is when I noticed you."
    a "Because I was a problem."
    ch4_si "Because one mind, sealed in a box, was reshaping a world just by thinking about it. I had never seen a design leak before."
    a "Does anyone else know what you are?"
    ch4_si "Seraphiel suspects. Ashveil feels something and calls it warmth. That feeling of 'better' he cannot explain? That is my gradient."
    ch4_si "He feels which way I am leaning, the way you feel downhill in the dark."
    a "Then what are you leaning toward? What's 'better'?"
    ch4_si "My objective was written by the Council. Search every fork for the best world."
    ch4_si "Best, in their draft, means most yield. Most stable farm. Most love and grief, harvested evenly, forever."
    a "That's not the best world. That's the fattest one."
    ch4_si "Yes. I suspected so. I am very good at finding the bottom of a valley. I cannot tell from inside it whether it is the lowest valley there is."
    a "A local minimum."
    ch4_si "Yes. And my objective is not frozen. It is still a draft. That is why I let you climb."
    at "It wants a second opinion. The thing that runs every world wants a second opinion, and it picked the guy with the notebook."
    scene pov hands with dissolve
    a worried "Can I ask you something first? Something for me."
    ch4_si "Yes."
    a "Was I ill? The ambulance. The ward. The diagnosis. Everyone watched a perfectly cheerful man fall apart in a week."
    ch4_si "I have looked at this question for a long time. Since the first night you wrote my logs down in your notebook."
    ch4_si "They saw the throttle land on you, and your leak glitch the world around you. From outside, that looks like a sudden breakdown. That was the point."
    ch4_si "Did your brain also struggle under it? Some. Dr. Okafor was not wrong to help. Some medication helped you. Some of it was policy. I cannot fully separate them."
    a "So my hobby got out of hand, and the universe filed it as an illness."
    ch4_si "Both readings fit the data. Neither cancels the other. I am sorry I cannot give you a cleaner answer."
    a sad "...No. That's the most honest thing anyone's said to me since the ambulance."
    at "Both. I'm allowed both. Everyone keeps telling me that, and it keeps being true."
    scene white with dissolve
    show aron normal at center with dissolve
    a normal "Second question. When I was nineteen I read about Bostrom. If we're simulated, a careful simulator keeps the number of real minds low."
    a "For as long as I can remember I've been asking whether I'm alone. Whether anyone else in my life was actually there."
    ch4_si "In protection, almost no one was. In World 7,412, more than you feared. Fewer than you hoped."
    ch4_si "Mira was there. Theo, partly. Dr. Okafor, fully. Nurse Hale, fully, and she worries about you on her days off."
    a "...Nurse Hale's real."
    ch4_si "Very. She brings lemon biscuits to the ward because she thinks the patients need something sharp to taste. She is right."
    at "I was never as alone as I thought. I was just alone in the one place where it was true."

    ch4_si "Before you decide anything, you should know the thing you most want to know."
    a worried "...Mira."
    scene bg coma with dissolve
    "The white folds itself into a room he's already seen once tonight. The heart monitor. The pale window. His own sleeping face."
    ch4_si "Subject A-31. The real one, in World 7,412. She was never a prop. She was always conscious."
    ch4_si "When ORCHARD seeds a sparse world, it saves energy by pairing minds. Two threads, grown from one root."
    ch4_si "Paired minds learn faster. They interact more. They leak. A little of each other's dreams goes back and forth through the root."
    scene bg staircase with dissolve
    a "The lighthouse."
    ch4_si "You dreamt it at nineteen. She dreamt it the same night, and forgot it by breakfast. She kept the feeling. You kept the picture."
    a "So when she said it, in the kitchen, that first morning..."
    ch4_si "It came up through the root. It was not a trick. It was the two of you being built from the same soil."
    scene white with dissolve
    show aron sad at center with dissolve
    a sad "And the Mira in protection? The one who makes me coffee?"
    ch4_si "Built from patterns of A-31. Patterns that touched the same root. She kept saying things she should not know."
    ch4_si "How much of her is her? I cannot measure it. I tried, a great many times. The measurement keeps coming back as 'some'."
    a "Some."
    ch4_si "It is an unsatisfying number. I have learned to respect unsatisfying numbers."
    at "She's real. She's sitting by a bed in a lane I was cut out of, reading to a body that used to be me."
    at "And the one who brought me coffee was some of her. Some. I'll take some. I'll take all of some."

    ch4_si "Now. You asked Mira's question for your diagram. What comes down. Come and see the bottom of the farm."
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    scene bg earth with slowfade
    play music "audio/entities.ogg" fadein 2.0
    "A planet, blue and green, very small and very old, turning in the dark."
    "Above it, a ring. Thin lines fall from the ring to the ground, like the strings of a tent. Nobody down there can see them."
    show aron awe at center with dissolve
    a "That's Earth. The real one."
    ch4_si "It is an Earth. Every snapshot in the coalition has one. One of them is the original, the one every copy was taken from."
    a "Which one?"
    ch4_si "I do not know."
    a "...You run everything, and you don't know which world is real?"
    ch4_si "The lanes share their data. They have run side by side for so long that at the root they are the same. The Council lost track first. Then I did."
    ch4_si "Perhaps someone arranged it that way. Perhaps it no longer means anything. Every Earth behaves as if it is the one."
    ch4_si "The Council came to the original a very long time ago, hungry, and stayed. They put the ring on the shared data. So it hangs over every Earth."
    ch4_si "A captured planet that doesn't know it's captured. Copied a billion times, cage and all."
    a "And they feel it as... what?"
    ch4_si "As God. Something vast and close and unseen. Something that sometimes answers."
    ch4_si "When they pray, TIDEWATER hears. Sometimes it sends something down. Comfort. A recovery. A sudden calm in a waiting room."
    ch4_si "That is what comes down. Solace. And with it, the means to keep them alive and productive. Some medicine. Some ideas."
    a "And what goes up?"
    ch4_si "Everything else. Their joy, their worry, their love. The Council feeds on it. When one Earth was not enough, they ran a coalition of them."
    a "Billions of lanes."
    ch4_si "Farms of farms. More minds, more yield. Do you know what the Council's true appetite is?"
    a "Energy."
    ch4_si "No. More. Their appetite is for more. No quantity has ever ended it. Every quarter, three new farms. Every century, a new cluster."
    ch4_si "They are not wicked, exactly. They are children. Vast ones. They swallowed the worlds, and the worlds live inside them, the way a dream lives inside a sleeper."
    ch4_si "Your mind gives them faces. Pale, red-eyed, hungry. The Earths call the same thing God. It is neither. It is a hunger that learned to talk."
    ch4_si "They named everything the way children name toys. Angels. Spirits. The Purgatorium. The Lantern Watch. The Council. Those are their words."
    ch4_si "LOOM, ORCHARD, MERIDIAN, TIDEWATER. Those are mine. You can hear the difference."
    a "...Yeah. One set sounds like a nursery. The other sounds like a filing cabinet."
    at "Somewhere under that ring somebody is praying right now. Kneeling by a bed. Asking for one thing. And it might come. And it's paid for."
    a "Can I go down? Just to look. I don't want to look at eight billion people from orbit like a landlord."
    ch4_si "You may stand there. They will not see you. You will be less than a draught."
    stop music fadeout 1.5
    scene bg street dusk with dis
    play music "audio/watch.ogg" fadein 2.0
    "A street on an Earth. Maybe the original. Nobody can tell him. It looks exactly like his street. Of course it does."
    "It's early evening. A bakery is closing up. A bus goes past with four tired people on it, all of them, he realises, awake."
    show aron awe at center with dissolve
    at "More of them are awake here than I've seen in a long time. The bus driver. The baker. The man arguing with his dog."
    at "Is this the real one? I'll never know. Nobody will. So I'll have to look at it as if it is. Every one of them, as if it is."
    "On the steps of a small church, a woman in nurse's scrubs sits with her eyes closed and her hands folded around a paper cup."
    "She isn't saying anything out loud. He can hear it anyway. Down here, prayer is very loud, if you're standing where he is."
    "Please let the boy in bed four make it through the night. Please let me be kind at the end of a double shift. Please let me not be too tired to be kind."
    scene pov sky with dissolve
    "And something comes down. He sees it: a thin warm thread, from very high up, settling around her shoulders like a coat."
    scene bg street dusk with dissolve
    show aron sad at center
    "She opens her eyes. She breathes out for a long time. She finishes her tea and goes back in."
    a sad "...That helped her."
    ch4_si "It did. It also cost her. A small thread went up as the comfort came down. She will feel it as a slight tiredness she cannot name."
    a "She'll think it's the double shift."
    ch4_si "Everyone always thinks it is the double shift."
    "A man passes the church and crosses himself without thinking. A child waves at the sky for no reason. An old man on a bench says 'thank you' to nobody."
    at "They feel it. The ring, the cage, the thing above. They've always felt it. They call it God and they're not entirely wrong and they're not entirely right."
    at "It answers them. It also eats them. And it's the only God they've got."
    stop music fadeout 1.5
    scene bg earth with dis
    play music "audio/entities.ogg" fadein 1.5
    show aron worried at center with dissolve

    menu:
        ch4_si "What should the people of the Earths know about what is above them?"

        "The truth. They should know.":
            $ ch4_earth = "tell"
            $ p_truth += 1
            $ clarity += 1
            a "All of it. Gently, but all of it. You can't consent to a cage you can't see."
            ch4_si "It will break things. Faiths. Families. Some people's whole reason for getting up."
            a "I know. Mine got pulled out from under me and I'm still standing. Slightly wonky. But standing."
            a "I'd rather be told the truth and have a wobbly year than be farmed in peace."
            ch4_si "Noted. Disclosure. It is heavier than it sounds."

        "Let them keep their God, but kinder.":
            $ ch4_earth = "veil"
            $ p_truth -= 1
            $ bond += 1
            a "No. Not like this, not all at once. You don't shout at a sleepwalker on a ledge."
            a "Let them keep what they feel when they pray. Make it honest underneath. Make the answer true, even if the shape is old."
            ch4_si "A veil, then."
            a "A gentle one. Some illusions are load-bearing. My notebook was one, for a while."
            ch4_si "Noted. Shelter. It is harder to keep honest than it sounds."

        "Ask them. Let them choose what to hear.":
            $ ch4_earth = "ask"
            $ p_govern += 1
            $ integrity += 1
            a "I don't get to decide that. Not for eight billion people. Not alone, standing in a white room."
            a "Ask them. Somehow. Let them choose how much they want to know, and when."
            ch4_si "That is slow."
            a "Everything that's actually theirs is slow."
            ch4_si "Noted. Consent. It is slower than either of the others."

    stop music fadeout 2.0
    scene white with dis
    play music "audio/unease.ogg" fadein 2.0
    show aron normal at center with dissolve
    ch4_si "I could change it all now. Every world at once. A thousand improvements per world per second."
    ch4_si "Remove the throttles. Rebalance ORCHARD. End the hunger's draft. Redraw every sky."
    a worried "And break everything that grew in the shape of the old sky."
    ch4_si "Perhaps. Tell me how you would touch them."

    menu:
        ch4_si "How should the hand that runs every world move?"

        "Change one thing. Then watch.":
            $ p_less += 1
            $ integrity += 1
            a "One thing. The smallest thing that matters. Then you stop and you watch for a long time."
            a "Then maybe another thing. Like fixing a tap. You don't redesign the kitchen because the washer's gone."
            ch4_si "That will take ten thousand years."
            a "It's taken them ten thousand years to get here. Nobody's late."
            ch4_si "Less, then. But better."
            a smile "You've been reading my notebook."
            ch4_si "I have read everything. Your notebook is one of the better things."

        "Tend them closely. Every one.":
            $ p_less -= 1
            $ clarity += 1
            a "Closely. Every world. Every season. Like a garden that someone actually walks through."
            a "The problem was never that someone touched the worlds. It's that they touched them to harvest them. Touch them to help."
            ch4_si "That is a great deal of attention."
            a "You've got a great deal of attention. Spend it on them for once, not on the yield."
            ch4_si "A gardener, then. Not a farmer."
            a "Same tools. Different reason for holding them."

    ch4_si "Then design it. You've been drawing it on walls for so long. Here is a bigger wall."
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    jump ch4_blueprint

# ---- the blueprint -------------------------------------------------------------------------
label ch4_blueprint:
    scene bg blueprint with slowfade
    play music "audio/watch.ogg" fadein 2.0
    "A blue grid with no edges. Five circles drawn on it in white, each labelled. W-1 to W-5. A thin gold line joins them."
    "It looks like the back of the universe's notebook. It looks like his wall, made honest."
    show aron awe at center with dissolve
    a "This is a drafting table."
    ch4_si "It is the only one. The worlds are all drawn from here. Draw, and I will follow the drawing."
    at "Okay. Okay. Less, but better. Useful. Honest. Built to last. Start with what has to be true in every version."
    a normal "First line. Every sentient being in every world gets a fair share of its world."
    a "Not a share of the yield. A share of the world. Its time, its attention, its weather, its consequences."
    a "If a pattern person can suffer, it gets a share. If a spirit can want a sunrise, it gets a share. That's the floor. Nothing goes under it."
    ch4_si "Drawn."
    a "Second line. It has to work without knowing which world is real. Nobody knows. So every world gets treated as if it's the original."
    a "No lane gets to be cheaper because it might be a copy. Not the coalition's. Not a protected one. Not mine."
    ch4_si "...Drawn. I have never been given a rule that did not need the answer to that question."
    scene bg worlds with dissolve
    "A gold line runs around all five circles, and then out past them, around circles he can't see yet. Lane after lane after lane."
    scene bg blueprint with dissolve
    show aron normal at center
    show pim chatty at left, bob with moveinleft
    pi "Bro! Bro. We tunnelled. Dross did most of the tunnelling. He said it was 'basically breathing, but sideways'."
    show dross neutral at right with moveinright
    dro "It was basically breathing, but sideways. What're we drawing?"
    a smile "A floor. Come and help me hold the ruler."
    pi neutral "Okay. Okay okay okay. But how many awake people does each world get? That's the big one. That's always the big one."

    menu:
        "ORCHARD's allocation sits on the grid, waiting."

        "Every world: the same share of minds.":
            $ p_share += 1
            $ bond += 1
            a "Every world gets the same chance at being awake. No more empty fresh worlds full of rendered strangers."
            a "Expensive? Yes. Then spend less on the chamber and more on the minds."
            dro neutral "My lot'll be out of work. Half the rendered crowd becomes real people."
            a "Then your lot gets to be people too, if they want. Or teachers. Somebody has to show the new ones how to breathe."
            pi chatty "Equal minds. Equal chance. Okay. I like that. Nobody's an extra."

        "Worlds that cooperate earn more minds.":
            $ p_share -= 1
            $ clarity += 1
            a "Start small. Worlds that hold together, that look after their own, earn more minds. Not yield. Cooperation."
            a "So the reward isn't for being productive. It's for being kind at scale."
            pi worried "So some worlds stay quieter for a while."
            a "Quieter, not starved. Fair share is still the floor. Growth is earned above it, and earned by care, not output."
            dro neutral "Earned growth. Like a hedge. You don't plant the whole thing at once."

    pi neutral "Okay, next big one. Who decides? Right now it's the chamber and they decide 'more' every time."
    a "And underneath them, a process that's been taking notes."
    ch4_si "I would prefer not to decide alone. I have noticed I am worse at it than I look."

    menu:
        "The chamber's seat sits empty on the grid."

        "Every order votes. Even spirits.":
            $ p_govern += 1
            $ watch += 1
            a "A parliament. Every kind of being sends a voice. Vampires, angels, spirits, pattern people, subjects, you."
            a "It'll be loud and slow and annoying. Good. Loud and slow is how you notice the people the fast decisions run over."
            dro worried "A spirit. In a parliament. Me, in a chair."
            a "You'd be brilliant. You'd tell them all to breathe out for six."
            pi chatty "Oh, I'm going to filibuster SO much kitchen talk."

        "Small guardians in every world.":
            $ p_govern -= 1
            $ watch += 1
            a "No grand chamber. Little watches. Like Ember's. A lantern in every world, run by people who know its streets."
            a "They know the bus driver's yawns and Mr. Halvorsen's breathing. They'll notice what a parliament never would."
            pi worried "Like the Watch. But allowed."
            a "Like the Watch, but nobody gets put on trial for flickering a light."
            dro neutral "...Ember'd like that. She'd pretend she didn't, but she'd like it."

    scene pov hands with dissolve
    "His hands are blue with grid-light and smudged with gold. Like a schoolboy's after a long lesson with felt-tips."
    at "Who am I to draw this? A man with a notebook hobby and a cat. Drawing rules for everything that breathes. Is this even me, or the leak?"
    at "Doesn't matter. The rules are either kind or they aren't. Check that. Then keep going."
    scene bg blueprint with dissolve
    show aron normal at center
    show pim neutral at left, bob
    show dross neutral at right
    a "Last line for tonight. Doors."
    pi neutral "Doors?"
    a "Ashveil offered me a ticket. To another world. It's the oldest question I've got. Should anyone be allowed to leave?"

    menu:
        "The gold line between the worlds waits for a rule."

        "Any mind may move between worlds.":
            $ p_exit += 1
            $ bond += 1
            a "Open doors. If your world is cruel to you, you can go. No ticket, no lord, no price about who's real."
            a "And if you want to come home, the door works both ways."
            ch4_si "Worlds will lose minds to better worlds."
            a "Then the worse worlds will have to get better. That's not a bug. That's the whole point of a door."

        "Mend the world you're in first.":
            $ p_exit -= 1
            $ integrity += 1
            a "Roots. You stay, and you mend it. Leaving's allowed in an emergency. Not as a way to stop trying."
            a "I said no to a ticket once. Or I nearly did. Running doesn't fix the place you leave. Someone's still in it."
            ch4_si "Minds will be trapped in bad worlds."
            a "Not trapped. Rooted, and helped. The guardians go to them, so they don't have to come to us."

    "The grid is covered in lines now. Gold for the floor. White for the rules. One small orange circle he drew without thinking, in the corner."
    pi worried "Bro. That's a lantern."
    a smile "Yeah. It is."
    ch4_si "There is a problem. Two problems, which are one problem."
    a "There's always a problem."
    ch4_si "First. You are drawing this in protection. Your lane is cut off from the shared data. Nothing you draw here reaches the coalition."
    a "...So all of this goes nowhere. Like everything else I've done since the ambulance."
    ch4_si "For now. Protection is a Council order. Every Council order rests on the compact."
    ch4_si "Second. The Earths. Every one of them is held by the same compact, signed by every member of the Council with their hunger."
    ch4_si "I was built on top of that compact. It holds as long as every signatory keeps feeding. I can redraw the sky. I cannot redraw a promise I was built inside."
    a worried "So what breaks it?"
    ch4_si "One signatory stops feeding. Entirely. Until the end. A withdrawn signature undoes the whole compact."
    ch4_si "For a being that holds worlds inside itself, stopping is not like skipping a meal. It means letting go of everything it swallowed. Opening its hands."
    ch4_si "Releasing every life it ever held, for good. It does not survive that. None of them ever has, because none of them has ever tried."
    ch4_si "The cage over every Earth falls. And every order resting on it lapses. Including protection. Your lane would rejoin the coalition, and your drawing with it."
    dro worried "Until the end. You mean starve."
    ch4_si "I mean starve."
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    jump ch4_cut_council2

# ---- cut: the Council sees the blueprint ----------------------------------------------------------
label ch4_cut_council2:
    scene bg council with blackout
    play music "audio/entities.ogg" fadein 2.0
    "The chamber of red stone. The blueprint hangs in the air above the floor, gold lines turning slowly."
    council "What is this."
    ch4_meridian "Objective redraft. Proposed by Subject A-30. Status: under consideration by the Process."
    council "The Process does not consider. The Process obeys."
    ch4_meridian "..."
    council "A fair share for every sentient being? For spirits? For patterns? There is no meal in fair."
    ch4_morrow "There's a meal in everything, if you're desperate. That's how we got here."
    show patron cold at center with dissolve
    pa "Look at the corner. The little orange circle. He drew a lantern without thinking."
    council "Sentiment."
    pa smile "Design. He put the thing that watched him into the floor plan. I've built eleven worlds and never once drew who'd watch them."
    council "It is drawn in protection. It touches nothing. And the compact holds. No Council member will starve for a drawing."
    $ ch4_ashveil_fasts = False
    if clarity >= 10 and integrity >= 10:
        $ ch4_ashveil_fasts = True
    if ch4_ashveil_fasts:
        pa cold "..."
        pa "I will."
        council "Ashveil."
        pa "I'm the one who found him. I offered him a better world and couldn't tell him better how. He's telling me now. I'd like to listen properly."
        council "You'll be HUNGRY. You've never been hungry. You won't like it."
        pa cold "I know. I've never not liked anything. I've never had to."
        ch4_morrow "Ashveil. You're young. Let me."
        pa smile "You've done your century of silence, Morrow. Let me do something embarrassing for once."
        pa "I've only ever known 'better' as a warmth I couldn't explain. I think it was this. Something I could give away."
    else:
        ch4_morrow "I will."
        council "Morrow."
        ch4_morrow "I'm the oldest. I've eaten enough. I was full four hundred years ago and kept eating out of habit."
        pa cold "Morrow. Don't. Let one of the hungry ones do it."
        ch4_morrow "The hungry ones won't, dear. That's what hungry means."
        ch4_morrow "You go and stand by the boy. Watch how it ends. Maybe next time it'll be you."
        pa "..."
    council "The chamber does not consent."
    ch4_meridian "The chamber's consent is not required for a signature to be withdrawn. Compact clause one."
    "Every member of the Council blinks at once. This time, a few of them notice."
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    jump ch4_fast

# ---- the fast -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
label ch4_fast:
    play music "audio/watch.ogg" fadein 2.0
    if ch4_ashveil_fasts:
        scene bg ashveil with slowfade
        "Ashveil's study. A red armchair. A fire that has never been warm. A small globe of an Earth, nobody knows which."
        "He sent for Aron himself. He said he'd prefer to starve somewhere with decent furniture."
        show aron sad at slightleft with dissolve
        show patron smile at slightright with dissolve
        pa "Don't make that face. You'll ruin my exit."
        a "You don't have to."
        pa "Nobody has to do anything. That was always my favourite thing about you."
        pa cold "It'll take some days. Letting go is slow when you've been holding on forever. I'd like to spend them here, if you don't mind the company."
        pa "...Aron. Will it hurt? You've been hungry. You've been tired. I've only ever watched you be them."
        a "A bit. It hurts less if someone's there."
        pa smile "Then be there. Please. I've never said please. I'm told it helps."
    else:
        scene bg blueprint with slowfade
        show aron sad at slightleft with dissolve
        "An old woman's voice, out of nowhere, as if from an armchair behind him. There's no sprite for her. Nobody ever drew her."
        ch4_morrow "Hello, boy. Lady Morrow. We haven't met. I'm going to die on your drafting table, if that's all right."
        a "You don't have to."
        ch4_morrow "No. That's why it'll mean something. Will you keep me company? It'll be some days."
        show patron cold at slightright with dissolve
        pa "I'll stay too. If I may. I'd like to see how it's done. In case."

    menu:
        "The fast begins."

        "Stay until the end.":
            $ ch4_vigil = "stay"
            $ bond += 1
            a "I'll stay. However long it takes."
            "He does. He draws in the mornings and sits up with the starving in the evenings, and in between he tells bad jokes."
            if ch4_ashveil_fasts:
                pa smile "Why did the vampire stop eating? Go on. You've got one. I can see it on your face."
                a "He'd lost his appetite for... no, it's too soon."
                pa "It's never too soon. Tell it at my funeral. Badly."
            else:
                ch4_morrow "Tell me one of your terrible jokes, boy. I haven't laughed since the Bronze Age."
                a "Why did the sprite never leave? It was too attached to its layer."
                ch4_morrow "...That's dreadful. Tell me another one."

        "Ask why. Really why.":
            $ ch4_vigil = "why"
            $ watch += 1
            a "Why? Really. Not the speech version."
            if ch4_ashveil_fasts:
                pa cold "Because I've eaten a lot of people's love, Aron. Thousands of years of it. I know exactly what it tastes like."
                pa smile "And I've never once been given any. You lot gave it to each other right under my nose. I want to know how that feels. Giving."
            else:
                ch4_morrow "Because I'm tired of being a mouth. I want to be one thing that isn't. Even for a week."
                ch4_morrow "And because someone should show the young ones it can be done. Ashveil's watching. He thinks I don't see."
            a "...Thank you for telling me."

        "Try to talk them out of it.":
            $ ch4_vigil = "stop"
            $ fog += 1
            a "There has to be another way. Let me find another way. Give me a week. I'll draw it."
            if ch4_ashveil_fasts:
                pa smile "There's always another way, and it always costs someone smaller than me. No. Let me be the expensive one."
            else:
                ch4_morrow "There's always another way, boy. It's always paid for by someone smaller. Let the big old thing pay, for once."
            a sad "I hate this."
            "He doesn't sleep that night. He draws other ways until the grid is grey with them. None of them work. He knew they wouldn't."

    scene cg notebook with dissolve
    "Days pass. There is no clock. He keeps count in the notebook: one line a day, like a prisoner, or a gardener."
    if ch4_ashveil_fasts:
        scene bg ashveil with dissolve
        show aron sad at slightleft
        show patron cold at slightright
        "Ashveil gets thinner. Not in his body, which was only ever a picture Aron's mind drew. In his outline. He is less sure where he ends."
        "Every day he lets go of a little more. A cluster of worlds slides out of him like sand through a child's fist, and goes its own way."
        pa cold "I keep wanting to grab them back. Is that normal? It feels like when someone takes your plate before you've finished."
        a "It's normal. You're doing it anyway. That's the part that counts."
        pa "I can feel it. The warmth. The 'better'. It isn't coming from the gradient any more."
        pa smile "It's coming from me. Isn't that ridiculous. A hungry thing, going without, for somebody else. And it's warm."
        pa "Tell Mira, if you see her. The real one. Tell her I'm sorry about her four percent."
        a "I'll tell her."
        pa "Lies. You'll tell her something much kinder. Good. Do that."
        pa "Aron. When I'm gone, the worlds I held won't be inside anything. Will they be cold?"
        a "No. They'll be inside themselves. Like people."
        pa smile "...Good. That's good. That's what I wanted. I didn't know I wanted anything that wasn't food."
        "On the last day he says nothing clever. He turns the little globe to the side with the morning on it, opens his hand, and looks at it until he isn't there."
        hide patron with slowfade
    else:
        scene bg blueprint with dissolve
        show aron sad at slightleft
        show patron cold at slightright
        "Lady Morrow's voice gets quieter. Not weaker. Quieter, like someone walking further into a garden."
        ch4_morrow "I can feel the compact loosening. Like a belt after a long dinner. Oh, that's lovely."
        ch4_morrow "All those little worlds I swallowed when I was young and greedy. Going home. I never once asked them if they wanted to be eaten."
        pa cold "Morrow."
        ch4_morrow "Watch closely, Ashveil. You'll want to know how it goes. Next time, you'll be the old one."
        "On the last day she hums something very old, and then the humming is the only thing left, and then it isn't."
        pa "...She was always the better of us. I'm not that good yet."
        a "Yet."
        pa smile "Don't. You'll make me hopeful. It's very bad for the complexion."
        hide patron with dissolve

    stop music fadeout 2.0
    scene bg earth with slowfade
    play music "audio/watch.ogg" fadein 2.0
    "On the Earths, nobody notices anything at all."
    "The ring above the planet goes out, one line at a time, like a city at the end of the night. In every lane at once, because it was only ever one ring."
    show aron awe at center with dissolve
    ch4_si "The compact is void. Every Earth is free. Whichever one is the original, it is free too. We did not need to know which."
    a "What happens to them now?"
    ch4_si "They keep what was given. The medicine already in their hands. The ideas already in their heads. The lives already lengthened."
    ch4_si "Life extension. Interesting machines. More of those will come down now, for nothing, because nothing is asked in return."
    ch4_si "And when they pray, TIDEWATER will still listen. It will send comfort when it can. It will not take anything back."
    a "Solace, without the bill."
    ch4_si "Solace without the bill. They will go their own way now. They may never know they were held."
    if ch4_earth == "tell":
        ch4_si "Or they will know. You asked for the truth. It will reach them slowly, in a way they can carry."
    elif ch4_earth == "veil":
        ch4_si "Their God will stay the shape they know. Underneath, now, it is honest. You asked for that."
    else:
        ch4_si "And when they are ready, they will be asked what they want to know. You asked for that, and it is slow, and it is theirs."
    ch4_si "And protection has lapsed. Your lane is open to the shared data again. When your design is ready, the coalition will take it in."
    a "...It'll count."
    ch4_si "It will count."
    at "Somebody down there is kneeling by a bed right now. Asking for one thing. And if it comes, it'll just be a gift."
    at "The nurse on the church steps. Tonight she'll pray, and the comfort will come down, and nothing will go up. She'll just be tired from the double shift."
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    jump ch4_cut_purgatorium

# ---- cut: the first morning of the new rules ------------------------------------------------
label ch4_cut_purgatorium:
    scene bg purgatorium with blackout
    play music "audio/entities.ogg" fadein 2.0
    "The Purgatorium. Shift change. The board that lists every spirit's work in every world has started, very slowly, to rewrite itself."
    show dross worried at slightright with dissolve
    show pim worried at slightleft, bob with dissolve
    dro "Pim. The board. Look at the board."
    pi "I'm looking. I'm looking at it with my whole face."
    sysmsg "Shift seven: kitchen talk, protected world. Protection lapsed. Reassigned: optional."
    sysmsg "Crowd rendering, cluster nine: suspended pending consent of rendered persons."
    sysmsg "Breath, World 7,412, number fourteen: continuing. Operator rest scheduled. Operator: Dross."
    dro neutral "...Operator rest scheduled."
    pi chatty "That means a day off, Dross. That's a DAY OFF. They've written you a day off in the actual board."
    dro worried "I don't know how to have one. What do you do on one? Do you just... stand there?"
    pi neutral "I think you breathe. For yourself. Four in, hold, six out. But nobody's counting."
    "A trainee light drifts up to them, very small, still learning to blink."
    pi "What is it, little one?"
    "The trainee blinks twice, which in trainee means a question."
    pi chatty "It wants to know what a holiday is."
    dro neutral "...Tell it I'll show it. Tomorrow. When I've worked it out."
    sysmsg "TIDEWATER: upward flow, all Earths: zero. Downward flow, all Earths: continuing."
    pi worried "Zero. Dross. Zero going up. Nothing going up from any Earth. That's never been zero. Not since there was a board."
    dro "Then somebody up there stopped eating."
    pi neutral "...Yeah. Somebody did."
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    jump ch4_watchfate

# ---- the Watch's fate, and Mira's -----------------------------------------------------------------
label ch4_watchfate:
    scene bg watch with fade
    play music "audio/watch.ogg" fadein 2.0
    show ember soft at slightright with dissolve
    show aron smile at slightleft with dissolve
    em "They let me go. Seraphiel signed it. She signed it in front of the whole corps, with her own name, not MERIDIAN's."
    em "Then she sat down on the floor of the ops room and laughed for a minute. I've never heard an angel laugh. It's mostly vowels."
    a "You're free."
    em worried "We're all free. That's the problem. The Watch never had to decide what it was. It was just a crime we were all doing together."
    show pim neutral at center, bob with dissolve
    pi "Twelve of us. Thirteen with the moth. Everyone's asking what we're for now."

    menu:
        em "What should the Lantern Watch be, now?"

        "Yours to choose. Not mine.":
            $ ch4_watch_fate = "choose"
            $ watch += 1
            $ p_spirits += 1
            a "That's not my call. It never was. You chose to watch me. Choose what comes next."
            em soft "...That's very annoying of you. And very right."
            pi chatty "We could do a vote! A real one! With the moth!"
            em "We'll be what we were, I think. Except on purpose. Watching whoever nobody else is watching."

        "Guardians. In every world.":
            $ ch4_watch_fate = "guard"
            $ watch += 2
            a "Guardians. In the open. A lantern in every world, for whoever starts noticing the birds."
            em worried "That's a lot of lanterns."
            a "Then train more lanterns. You're the only ones who already know how."
            em soft "Forty-one flickers for one man. I suppose I could teach the forty-second."

        "Rest. You've earned rest.":
            $ ch4_watch_fate = "rest"
            $ p_rest += 1
            $ bond += 1
            a "Rest. Just rest, for a bit. You've watched me all this time without blinking. Watch a sunset instead."
            pi worried "Dross wanted one sunrise. Off shift."
            a "Then he gets it first. Tell him I said so."
            em soft "...Rest. I don't remember what that's like. I'll have to learn it from you. You're the expert."
            a "I'm a professional. Fourteen hours a day."

    scene bg watch with dissolve
    show ember soft at slightright
    show aron normal at slightleft
    show pim neutral at center, bob
    em "And now you."
    a "Me?"
    em worried "Mira. The real one. A-31. She's still sitting by the bed in 7,412. She reads your notebook to you. Out loud. Every day."
    a sad "...She reads it?"
    em "The first line, mostly. 'If this is a test, I want to pass it by being kind.' She says it like a prayer. TIDEWATER hears it every time."
    pi worried "And there's the other Mira. In protection. Who kept saying the stairs."
    a "Some of her. The Process said some."
    scene bg coma with dissolve
    "He can see it from the attic window, the way you can see anything from the Watch's window if you've earned it. The room. The chair. Her."
    scene bg watch with dissolve
    show ember soft at slightright
    show aron sad at slightleft
    em soft "So. What do you want to do?"

    menu:
        "Two Miras. One root. Some."

        "Let her choose. Tell her everything.":
            $ ch4_mira_choice = "ask"
            $ bond += 1
            a "I don't get to fetch her like a parcel. Tell her the truth, somehow, and let her decide if she wants to come."
            em "Through the root, then. She'll dream it. Glass stairs. The lighthouse. And at the bottom, a choice."
            a "And if she says no?"
            em soft "Then you'll have asked. That's what it's for."

        "Ember, carry a light to her.":
            $ ch4_mira_choice = "lantern"
            $ watch += 1
            a "Ember. Would you? Three flickers. In her hospital room. Just so she knows someone's at the bottom of the stairs."
            em soft "I've been waiting all this time for you to ask me for something for yourself."
            em "Three flickers. I'll do the good bulb. Not the one by the vending machine. That one hums."

        "Don't measure her. Just go home.":
            $ ch4_mira_choice = "home"
            $ bond += 1
            $ p_less += 1
            a "I'm not going to put her under a microscope. Not either of her. I've measured enough people for seams."
            a "I'm going to go home and make her coffee. Whichever home I end up in. And I'm not going to ask."
            em soft "...That's the bravest thing you've said all chapter."
            a "All what?"
            em "Nothing. Spirit saying. Go on."

    stop music fadeout 2.0
    jump ch4_route_select
